From 936cf868da21acb90c77bc549133451a27c8f44b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 17:51:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0270 -- #3: cache the Pixtone SFX render output (skip
 the ~51s boot synth)

On a Pentium-class DOS box, Pixtone::init() (SB16/OPL3/organya DAC) and
Pixtone::initGusSfx() (GF1) each synthesise all 0x75 (117) fxNN.pxt from
scratch at boot via stPXSound::render() -- the per-sample wavetable synth.
That is ~51 s of pure CPU, paid on EVERY launch and identical across all
audio backends (both init paths run the same render()). The operator quits
thinking the game hung.

The organya PCM cache (patch 0215 / ORG_AUTOCACHE) already solves this shape
for music -- render once, persist, load next boot -- but it is organya-only;
Pixtone was never cached. This caches the render() OUTPUT
(stPXSound::final_buffer, int8_t S8 mono @ 22050 Hz), which is
TIER-INDEPENDENT and feeds BOTH backends (init() resamples it to the runtime
S16 tier; initGusSfx() uploads it to GF1 DRAM). One tier-independent blob
CACHE\PXT\PXTSFX.BIN {header magic 'PXC1' + build SHA12 + num_sounds; per-slot
index; concatenated S8 PCM} thus skips the 51 s render on every backend and
every tier, and is the smallest possible artifact.

First launch renders every slot once + writes the blob (still ~51 s, once);
subsequent launches load the blob and skip render entirely. Keyed to the full
DOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12 in file CONTENT (a rebuild that changes the synth math or
NUM_SOUNDS invalidates); like ORG_AUTOCACHE, a .pxt swap without a rebuild does
not invalidate (accepted + documented). fopen is always "rb"/"wb" (DJGPP text
mode would corrupt the binary PCM). Best-effort write: a full / read-only CF
logs + removes any partial blob and re-renders next boot.

Killswitch: default-ON; disabled only by the exact string
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_PXT_AUTOCACHE=0 (strict-killswitch idiom, mirrors
ORG_AUTOCACHE / PIXTONE_IRQ_MIX). Off = byte-identical boot, just slow.

The GF1 loop now consumes cached PCM via a non-owning stPXSound view, so its
per-slot load()/RENDERSAFE-render-skip/render() steps + the fx6e/fx6d
render/load heap breadcrumbs (patch 0257, triaging a now-FIXED crash) are gone;
the UPLOAD-path crash guards (0242 pad / 0247 bracket / 0256 straddle) and
render()'s own 0246 OOM-silence guard are preserved. The cache is built from a
FULL render of every slot so a GUS-only first boot still produces a complete,
reusable cache; the music-priority budget still governs GF1 uploads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
